  "semantics": "Opening applies global defaults once. Successful Calculate saves the used custom/raw/log/mode choices, independently remembering basic area-selection and scientific ROI policies. Custom bins/bounds are updated only for a successful custom calculation. Raw calculations preserve prior custom defaults and ignore invalid hidden custom text. Scientific reopening uses Current at the new source pose; indices, numeric ranges, ROI geometry and output paths are not global defaults.",
  "validation": "Bounds are a finite increasing pair, validated atomically with the full Settings patch. Migration processes supplied bounds together instead of rejecting a valid lower endpoint in lexical order; invalid pairs recover together to 0..1 with warnings/write protection. Histogram group reset preserves other settings.",
  "publication": "Native calculation, formatted values, provenance, shared immutable result allocation and settings patch are staged before the remember callback. Preferences save and in-memory preference swap precede allocation-free result ownership/JSON/string moves. A save I/O failure preserves prior result/defaults; protected implicit saves preserve file bytes while allowing session defaults/result update. Unknown preference compartments survive successful saves. No cross-provider/RSS transaction is claimed.",
  "verification": "1300 selected checks per OS including 124 new histogram preference checks. Independent readers verify 200 reports / 28368 physical-input frames, including 8 paired configure/inspect restart reports / 516 frames across standalone C++ and Python hosts. Counts, persisted choices, readonly source state, source-relative Current reopening, opaque retention and no-save inspection are checked. Six native executable suites per OS and fresh installed settings/preferences SDK consumers pass. Existing histogram/grid/threshold/settings/preference regressions remain. No complete upstream/resource/real-GPU platform acceptance.",
